WEBVTT

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:31.590
Banri!

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.480
Mother!

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.070
You took so long, Mother!

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.730
I've been painting so you could tell, and so many of them too!

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:41.340
What took you so long?!

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.000
I heard you were going to Hakumei's residence, so I thought you were safe.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.790
All these... Don't tell me that little child painted them all?

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:00.930
What an incredible talent.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:05.420
So, how did you come to be locked up here?

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:08.560
When I was walking to Uncle Hakumei's residence,

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:14.200
this stranger said that if I went to his place,
I'd be able to practice painting as much as I liked.

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.780
I was really happy.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.680
I tried hard, but I still couldn't reach your level, Mother.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.340
If I don't get better at drawing,
you'll leave me behind, like you did Father.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:37.750
Wh-What are you saying? I didn't leave him behind.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:41.220
That oaf is just taking too long to catch up with me!

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.210
To catch up...

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.200
Don't tell me he was...

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:53.500
I just wanted to paint like you.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.270
To make a painting like yours.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:03:01.280
No, I thought I wanted to draw something of my own, something that only I could draw.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:06.070
But I started to think that something was wrong.

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:11.620
The room was locked, and I wasn't
allowed to go outside this residence.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.930
It's all right. Everything's fine.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.200
You didn't do anything wrong.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:22.240
I just wanted you to notice, so bit by bit, I added my own style to the paintings.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:28.770
I knew they were up to something bad when they made me paint copies of originals.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:32.270
So you did it on purpose?

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.520
Yeah. I knew Mother would recognize it.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.740
So that's why Karin-san's been looking for all the forgeries since yesterday.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.150
She ran around town at incredible speed, didn't she?

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.770
Like a boar.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.040
Yeah.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.790
Really?! You really looked that hard for me?

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:54.620
Of course, but I just couldn't find you.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:58.800
However, when I saw this painting, I knew you had to be here.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.070
Oh, I painted that one!

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.450
It's a painting of this place based on what I could see from the window.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.330
That's why she was looking for the tree specialist and the gardener.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:12.910
I asked everywhere if anyone knew the garden depicted in this painting!

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:15.440
It took a while, but I finally found it.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.650
Judging from this conversation...

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.830
Yeah, there's no mistake.

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:22.230
I couldn't believe it at first, but Heki Yuukoku is...

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:40.340
This is...

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.280
A mold for counterfeit coins.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:48.600
Banri, don't tell me you carved this, too?

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:55.010
Y-Yeah. They suggested I try carving for a change.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:05:00.950
You're good at carving, so I thought I'd try it myself and made a few.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:04.070
They took the best one away, though.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.570
Umm, I mean...

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.580
I don't believe this.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:14.220
What? What's wrong?

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:16.900
Counterfeiting money is a serious crime.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:19.370
Regardless of whether a child was responsible, or someone else,

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.750
they'll be sentenced to death, without exception.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:33.370
Heki Yuukoku made all the forgeries and the counterfeit money.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.690
Heki Yuukoku is responsible for all of it, Your Highness.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.440
High-

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:44.440
Mother, Yuukoku isn't my pseudonym, it's yours.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:50.090
Banri, listen carefully. I have to leave you now and go on a long journey.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:54.830
Hakumei will care for you for the time being, and you're to go home when Dad arrives.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.370
Wh-Why?!

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:00.290
Was it because bad people kidnapped me?!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.840
Is that why you're angry at me?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.590
I'm sorry. I won't do it again, so please don't leave me!

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.090
Let me stay with you, please!

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:12.870
Mother!

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.860
I don't want you to leave!

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.280
It's all right.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.250
There's no need for the two of you to be separated.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.620
This is just a trial piece.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:39.550
What?

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:45.210
I've been searching for a well-known artist called Heki Yuukoku,

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.180
since I plan to issue new coins that are harder to forge.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:52.760
Not many know that he's as talented a carver as he is a painter.

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:58.570
Therefore, I asked you, Heki Yuukoku, to create molds for new coins.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:01.770
You accepted my request and began to carve molds.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:04.730
This is one of the trial pieces.

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:06.780
Isn't that right, Heki Yuukoku-dono?

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:09.280
You...

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:13.280
It's true that we were looking for you to make just such a request.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.110
I wanted to announce officially that new coins would be issued,

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:20.210
before the forged coins were mass-produced.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:25.570
If we asked Heki Yuukoku to create a mold, the quick-witted would catch on.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:30.860
That's why, officially, we were searching for you to ask for a portrait.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:35.720
It didn't quite happen in that order, but how about it?

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.870
I have no choice but to accept.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.360
No, I should really express my gratitude.

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:47.750
Thank you.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.360
Mother, don't leave me, please!

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:56.030
Banri...

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.070
You're making a funny face!

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:00.500
I'll paint that face for you later.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:00.500
What?!

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:02.740
You're so mean, Mother!

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.340
I'm just a subject for your work?!

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:07.690
To me, to paint is to live!

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:07.690
I don't want that!

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:09.000
It's only natural!

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.090
Your work is always more important than me!

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.010
That's harsh.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:13.630
But the boy has stopped crying.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.800
It's amazing how watching children never bores me!

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.850
Wh-What's going on?

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.930
Why are you people trespassing in my house?!

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.260
Oh, Dad.

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:24.560
S-S-Suou,

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:25.820
what's going on?

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:29.030
Dad, your humble moneymaking venture's been revealed, that's what's going on.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:29.820
What?

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:32.480
The art dealer who's been selling the forgeries

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:35.850
must've been caught at Heki Hakumei's residence by now.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.880
When I got home in the afternoon, I lied to him and said,

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:42.660
"Heki Hakumei wants one of this kid's paintings for his collection."

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.940
He dashed off as soon as I finished talking.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.820
Wh-What?!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.120
What's going on?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.010
This means that Tan-tan's father is the cause of all...

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.720
In that case, I've...

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:01.230
Tan-tan...

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.770
Oh, I realized it as soon as I saw the forgery up close.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:11.910
Dad's stupid like me, so he's been proudly displaying the originals in the house.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:15.860
You were the one who said,

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.020
"The person with the original is the most likely suspect."

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:24.420
By the way, Dad was in the Arts Department until recently.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:28.120
He was fired for losing a treasured painting, but now that I think about it,

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:32.200
he's been bringing them home to make forgeries.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.130
Suou... you...

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.040
This is my repayment, Kou Shuurei.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:42.110
If you write up this case in detail, instead of just filing a report, and present it to the Imperial Court,

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:44.890
your suspension might be lifted sooner.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:47.640
Tan-tan...

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:52.930
But you know, I think Dad didn't know about the counterfeit money at all.

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:53.940
Counterfeit money?!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:58.180
My Dad's a coward, so I doubt he'd go that far.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:09:59.780
I mean, if you're caught...

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.030
It's a death sentence.

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:06.540
To go that far...

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.920
What? What counterfeit money?!

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.310
I know nothing about that!

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:13.390
You won't be excused for "not knowing," will you?

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:16.490
They probably just took advantage of him.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:18.300
Took advantage of him?

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:22.510
When Dad told me that a higher official had ordered him to make me propose to you,

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:25.940
Dad was happy about the chances for riches and rank,

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:28.440
but I thought, "This sounds dodgy."

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:30.520
A higher official?

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:34.400
I don't know who, and my Dad probably doesn't either.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:38.390
The marriage was a fake, to force you to resign.

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:42.910
Whether it worked or not, I guess Dad and I would've been knocked off anyway.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.430
If you knew all that, why did you play along?!

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.560
Because it was all just a hunch.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:52.600
In the meantime, these incidents with the
forgeries and counterfeit money happened.

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:54.040
It was all too much of a coincidence.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.580
That's why I decided to bring the curtain down on this of my own accord.

00:10:57.580 --> 00:11:00.000
It was going to happen sooner or later, right?

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.760
Kouyuu, do you think something can be done about this?

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:08.800
Well, if we arrest them all in Your Highness name,

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:11.200
and unravel all the threads behind this case, then maybe...

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.560
Umm, I reckon that's probably useless.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.820
'Cause... they're here.

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:24.070
What is this?

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:26.280
Your Highness?!

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.580
The Section of Government Inspection has ordered us to arrest the perpetrators.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.990
Our orders are to arrest

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:38.210
Shin Ensai and Shin Suou immediately for the crimes of forgery and counterfeiting.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:44.340
You must be Shin Suou.

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:45.640
Yup.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.350
Then pardon me.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:51.060
Ouch!

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:55.060
As ordered, we will confiscate all of this as part of the indemnity.

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:57.130
Huh? Why?

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:01.780
Could it be... that fishy street vendor...

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.410
Was he an undercover inspector?!

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:05.910
I see.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:10.120
He was an undercover inspector too.

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:15.010
To ensure that the Shin family's money wasn't lost before they seized everything as an indemnity,

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:18.880
they deliberately sold expensive jewelry to Tan-tan-kun.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:22.240
Our orders are also to bring
Heki Karin-sama and Heki Banri-sama,

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:24.130
who were victims in this case,

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.840
under our protection with the utmost care.

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:29.850
How... How did they know about that as well?!

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:42.610
Wait!

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:44.610
What are the charges against him?!

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:48.970
Those involved in counterfeiting money are sentenced to death. That's the law.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.490
See, I told you, didn't I?

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:54.370
Society won't go easy on you.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:58.380
A crime is a crime, I suppose you could say.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:00.800
But...

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:05.470
Right now, you look like an ordinary girl.

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:29.760
So as we suspected, the inspectors went to Rin-dono's place that night as well?

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:35.500
Yes. She said that all the documents she'd been compiling for Shuurei-dono were confiscated.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:41.750
It seems they took the initiative to snatch whatever Shuurei had discovered.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.130
I see.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:50.890
Also, another thing is bothering me. We haven't found the best mold.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:52.640
Yeah.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:57.680
Excuse me!

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:04.680
Please accept my apologies for the trouble my sister and the others have caused!

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:09.910
Ah, no. You helped us a lot with this case. I'm the one who should thank you.

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.160
Not at all!

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:18.410
Umm... didn't my sister... say something... rude... to you?

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.500
Shoo! Get lost!

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.010
I-I knew it!

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:27.710
I am deeply sorry!

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:29.510
Never mind. Don't worry about it.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:34.010
By the way, how did Karin know I was the Emperor?

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:36.890
Ah, by phrenology.

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:43.150
If you're from an established family,
my sister can tell which one you come from.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.150
That's impressive.

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:53.780
Huh?

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:55.680
Tan-tan! You're not dead?!

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:58.410
What?

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:01.890
Don't tell me you broke into the prison?!

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:03.420
Of course not!

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.490
We went through all the official procedures...

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:09.460
and came here.

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:13.680
Oujo-sama made every effort to prove your innocence first.

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:17.770
Unlike your father, there was only
circumstantial evidence against you,

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.830
so we forced our way in and got you discharged.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:20.940
Wow.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:23.350
Tan-tan...

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.690
Why on earth didn't you try to defend yourself?! Not even a word!

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.480
Idiot! Raccoon! Tan-tan!

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:32.370
At least say, "I didn't do it!"

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:35.950
But, my Dad was involved!

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:40.960
Your previous rank's been revoked, but you're still hanging in there as joukan!

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:45.300
So, if you render some distinguished service before your father's execution date,

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:48.150
his sentence might be remitted.

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:53.700
Also, you can go back to your residence now, Tan-tan.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:57.240
The Heki family paid off some of the indemnity.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.470
Apparently, Banri-kun worked hard for it.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:02.460
You used to play with him, didn't you, Tan-tan?

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:08.230
Play... It was more like I kept him company.

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:11.910
Now and then, he used to stare out of the window and start crying, so...

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:14.820
Come to think of it, he drew a portrait of me once.

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:18.630
That might be worth a fortune in the future.

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:21.870
Well, for now, why don't you take it easy at home?

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:24.500
If you get lonely, you can come over to our place.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:29.780
Yes, if you give us that portrait by Banri-kun as an accommodation fee, I'll welcome you.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.760
A devil... That's what he is.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:38.620
See, if you're with us, Seiran becomes more outgoing. He even makes jokes like that.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:44.210
No way. I'd just get dragged around and be the target of bamboo shoots from your scary family retainer!

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:45.600
What are you talking about?

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:47.920
Seiran wouldn't do something like that, right?

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.700
Of course not, oujo-sama.

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:52.030
There seems to be an unfortunate misunderstanding between us.

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:53.840
Like I said...

00:16:57.680 --> 00:16:59.220
Huh? What's wrong, Tan-tan?

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:03.710
Umm... yeah... I might... come by...

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.230
What we were talking about last time?

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:09.970
What was it again?

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:13.720
Remember that time we went to see Kochou-san together?

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:15.850
Oh, that time!

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:18.070
You said something about making a proposal.

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:25.600
Shuurei, please be my wife.

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:33.150
Thanks, Santa...

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:36.900
"But" is what you're about to say, isn't it?

00:17:38.930 --> 00:17:42.520
Hey Santa, what you told me the other day...

00:17:42.520 --> 00:17:47.440
You said it so honestly, with no fancy words, that it pierced my heart.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.520
I won't take those words back.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:52.500
I know.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:55.990
I won't deny what you said either. I think you're right.

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:59.010
But you'd still rather be a government official.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:02.310
I want to be an Imperial official.

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:05.890
Right now, I want to take that path as far as I can go.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:09.310
That's why, Santa...

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:12.300
No, I won't listen to what you're about to say.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:13.900
Save it.

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:15.520
Save it?

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:18.390
It wasn't fair of me to say this, so I didn't until now,

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.870
but I'm leaving for Sashuu today.

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:21.510
What?!

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:22.660
Wh-Why?

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:24.910
It's partly your fault, you know.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.660
A while ago, some doctors used the Sashuu government

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:31.560
to make an announcement to the Merchants Guild.

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:36.260
They're seeking young researchers to develop alcohol suitable for sterilization.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:38.040
I came today, so that if you had said yes,

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:41.300
I could go to Uncle Shouka and Seiran straight away,

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:44.340
tell them formally, and take you to Sashuu with me.

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:51.290
But if it looked like you were going to refuse,
I'd pretend I didn't hear and run off to Sashuu.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:52.930
Wh-Why?

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:55.780
I have no intention of giving up so easily.

00:18:56.980 --> 00:19:00.150
I'll come back when I've become a good match for you.

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:03.160
Santa...

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:05.060
This is for you.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:06.070
What is it?

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:08.180
The first batch of sake I've ever made.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.260
Don't keep it. Drink it, okay?

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:16.170
Thanks, Santa.

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:18.520
Let me just say this.

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:23.050
When I get back, make sure you call me Keichou.

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:24.550
See you.

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:31.350
That was a surprise.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:35.310
He's a much harder suitor to brush off than Tan-tan.

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:41.610
Hey, Seiran, if he'd come to talk to you, would you have punched him?

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.870
Of course. I'd have left him more dead than alive.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.680
You're scary when you get angry.

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:50.870
I better not get married, for his sake.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:58.630
Oujo-sama, do you remember what you said a long time ago?

00:19:58.630 --> 00:19:59.870
You once said,

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:02.090
"I'm going to be Prime Minister in the future,

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:05.220
so Seiran had better become a general and kick the Emperor's butt.

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.970
Together we'll protect this country!

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:09.760
That's why, Seiran, you must work hard and get promoted!"

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:11.120
Like that.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:14.400
I-I might have said that.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.830
I hesitated a little.

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:26.930
Should I say that somehow I couldn't leave... or couldn't just sit by...

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:27.950
What?

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:35.000
I thought I might just get myself promoted a little higher.

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:40.500
Then I'll shift the menu from vegetables to meat right away!

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:41.940
I'll revise the account books.

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:45.810
Oh, but you might be so busy that you won't have time to eat with us.

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:47.730
Don't worry about that.

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:50.580
I'd come home if you were going to be there, oujo-sama.

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:51.390
Really?

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:54.890
You seem happier than I expected.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:21:01.910
Because my father and I can finally walk along with you, rather than be a burden to you!

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:18.990
Welcome!

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:22.930
Thank you for waiting.

00:21:25.190 --> 00:21:27.180
I heard your cherry tree is blooming.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:29.640
Yes. Just three blossoms, though.

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:49.140
I won't apologize to you.

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:52.370
Yes, there's no need for that.

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:58.090
I won't apologize, and if need be, I might do the same thing again.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:00.010
I know.

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:03.590
That's the Emperor's job.

00:22:08.730 --> 00:22:11.540
From here on, it will be Shi Ryuuki speaking.

00:22:11.540 --> 00:22:12.200
What?

00:22:14.760 --> 00:22:16.660
I know the Emperor.

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:19.650
If there's anything you want to tell him, I'll do it.

00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:29.660
Fine.

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.440
Then tell him this.

00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:33.160
Okay.

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:37.680
You bastard! Suspension?! Cut the crap!

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:46.710
That'll do. That's all there is.

00:22:47.520 --> 00:22:49.250
Tell that to the Emperor.

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:51.430
Is that all?

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:52.340
Yes.

00:22:52.340 --> 00:22:56.850
Anyway, I've made the vegetable dishes from Sashuu, as I promised.

00:22:56.850 --> 00:22:58.600
You'll try them, won't you?

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:00.880
Yes, I will!

00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:01.930
The spicy radishes?

00:23:01.930 --> 00:23:03.230
I didn't put them in.

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:04.020
The erhu?

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:05.550
Any piece you like.

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:06.460
A stroll?

00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:08.980
So long as it's within this garden.

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:09.850
Marry me.

00:23:09.850 --> 00:23:12.180
I don't remember promising you anything about that.

00:23:18.530 --> 00:23:20.850
Wh-What's so funny?!

00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:23.960
Shuurei's mean!

00:24:45.300 --> 00:24:47.410
This is bad, really bad, Tan-tan!

00:24:47.410 --> 00:24:51.210
If a joukan doesn't find a job within a month, he's fired!

00:24:51.210 --> 00:24:52.510
We've got to do something.

00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:57.300
Yet, how come all the other joukan aren't showing any interest?!
